---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Power BI Licence Calculator"
  description="Work out what Power BI actually costs for your team: Pro at $14, Premium Per User at $24, or a mix. Enter headcount and see the yearly total."
>
  <article class="calc">
    <div class="content-width">
      <span class="page-eyebrow">Tool</span>
      <h1>What will Power BI cost your team?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Enter how many people build reports and how many only read them. The
        calculator works out Pro, Premium Per User, and the mix most teams
        actually end up on.
      </p>

      <section class="inputs">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="creators">People who build and publish reports</label>
          <input id="creators" type="number" min="0" max="5000" value="3" inputmode="numeric" />
          <p class="hint">Authors, analysts, anyone opening Power BI Desktop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="viewers">People who only view reports</label>
          <input id="viewers" type="number" min="0" max="20000" value="17" inputmode="numeric" />
          <p class="hint">Sales, ops, managers reading dashboards in the browser.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="field field-check">
          <label>
            <input id="premium" type="checkbox" />
            <span>We need Premium features</span>
          </label>
          <p class="hint">
            Models over 1 GB, more than 8 refreshes a day, deployment pipelines,
            or AI features.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="results" aria-live="polite">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Option</th>
              <th>Per user / month</th>
              <th>Monthly</th>
              <th>Yearly</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="verdict" id="verdict"></p>
        <p class="checked">US list prices, checked 2 November 2026. Confirm in the Microsoft 365 admin centre before budgeting.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="notes">
        <h2>How the numbers work</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Power BI Free can't view shared reports.</strong> This is the
          part people miss. A Free account can open Power BI Desktop and build
          something locally, but the moment a report is published to the
          service, every viewer needs a licence — Pro, PPU, or a Fabric
          capacity. There is no "just share the link" option outside a
          capacity.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Pro is the default.</strong> At $14 per user per month it
          covers publishing, sharing, scheduled refresh and row-level security.
          Most teams under a few hundred people never need anything else.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>PPU is for the two or three people who hit the ceiling.</strong>
          It includes everything in Pro plus larger models, more frequent
          refreshes and the premium-only features. Buying it for the whole team
          is usually waste.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Fabric capacity is a different purchase.</strong> A capacity
          (F64 and up) lets Free users view reports, but it is billed monthly at
          a level that only pays off past roughly 300 users. The exact price
          varies by region and SKU, so this calculator doesn't guess at it —
          get a quote from Microsoft or a partner before going down that road.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>

        <h3>Q: Why does the calculator ask for two headcounts?</h3>
        <p>
          Because the two groups can sit on different licences. Only people who
          publish need PPU when premium features are required; viewers can stay
          on Pro. Asking for one total hides that saving, which is usually the
          single biggest line item.
        </p>

        <h3>Q: Do viewers need Pro if the report is in a Premium workspace?</h3>
        <p>
          Not if the workspace is backed by a Fabric capacity (F64 or above).
          In that case Free users can view. That is the only scenario where Free
          works for viewers, and it is why large organisations buy capacity
          instead of licences.
        </p>

        <h3>Q: Are these list prices?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes — US list prices, checked against Microsoft's Power BI pricing
          page on 2 November 2026. Enterprise agreements, non-profit and
          education pricing all differ. Always confirm in the Microsoft 365 admin
          centre before committing to a budget.
        </p>

        <h3>Q: What about Power BI Embedded or Report Server?</h3>
        <p>
          Embedded is for putting reports inside your own application and is
          priced per capacity, not per user — out of scope here. Report Server
          is an on-premises product with its own licensing. Neither maps cleanly
          onto the Pro/PPU decision above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="read-next">
        Want the reasoning rather than the arithmetic?
        <a href="/tutorials/power-bi-licensing-explained/">The full licensing guide</a>
        covers what each tier actually does and the mistakes that inflate the bill.
      </p>

      <p class="source">
        Prices from Microsoft's
        <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/products/power-bi/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Power BI pricing page</a>,
        checked 2 November 2026. Not affiliated with Microsoft.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // 价格核对日期：2026-11-02，来源为 Microsoft 官方 Power BI 定价页。
  // 改价时只改这里，并在页面上更新时间。
  const PRICE = { pro: 14, ppu: 24 };
  const BUILD = new Date("2026-11-02");

  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement | null;
  const money = (n: number) =>
    n.toLocaleString("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD", maximumFractionDigits: 0 });

  function render() {
    const creators = Math.max(0, parseInt($("creators")?.value || "0", 10) || 0);
    const viewers = Math.max(0, parseInt($("viewers")?.value || "0", 10) || 0);
    const premium = !!$("premium")?.checked;
    const total = creators + viewers;
    const rows = document.getElementById("rows");
    const verdict = document.getElementById("verdict");
    if (!rows || !verdict) return;

    if (total === 0) {
      rows.innerHTML = `<tr><td colspan="4" class="empty">Enter at least one person.</td></tr>`;
      verdict.textContent = "";
      return;
    }

    const options = [
      {
        name: "All Pro",
        per: PRICE.pro,
        seats: total,
        note: "Cheapest unless you need premium features.",
      },
      {
        name: "All Premium Per User",
        per: PRICE.ppu,
        seats: total,
        note: premium ? "Premium for everyone — rarely necessary." : "You didn't tick premium, so this is overspending.",
      },
      {
        name: "Mixed: PPU for builders, Pro for viewers",
        per: null,
        seats: null,
        note: "Builders get premium features, viewers pay Pro rates.",
        monthly: creators * PRICE.ppu + viewers * PRICE.pro,
      },
    ];

    rows.innerHTML = options
      .map((o) => {
        const monthly = o.monthly ?? (o.per as number) * (o.seats as number);
        const yearly = monthly * 12;
        const perLabel = o.per ? `$${o.per}` : "mixed";
        return `<tr>
          <td><strong>${o.name}</strong><br><span class="row-note">${o.note}</span></td>
          <td>${perLabel}</td>
          <td>${money(monthly)}</td>
          <td>${money(yearly)}</td>
        </tr>`;
      })
      .join("");

    const mixed = creators * PRICE.ppu + viewers * PRICE.pro;
    const allPro = total * PRICE.pro;
    const allPpu = total * PRICE.ppu;

    // 勾了 Premium 之后「全 Pro」根本用不了，不该参与比价 ——
    // 否则计算器会推荐一个满足不了需求的方案。
    // 边界：creators=0 时 mixed 与 allPro 完全相同（没有 builder 需要 PPU），
    // 此时宣称 "Mixed saves you $0 ... 0 builders on PPU" 是误导，直接推荐 All PPU。
    const mixedIsTrivial = creators === 0;
    const candidates = premium
      ? (mixedIsTrivial ? [allPpu] : [allPpu, mixed])
      : [allPro, allPpu, mixed];
    const cheapest = Math.min(...candidates);

    if (!premium && cheapest === allPro) {
      verdict.innerHTML = `<strong>All Pro is cheapest</strong> at ${money(allPro * 12)} a year. Nothing you described needs a premium licence.`;
    } else if (cheapest === mixed) {
      verdict.innerHTML = `<strong>Mixed licensing saves you ${money((allPro - mixed) * 12)} a year</strong> ` +
        `compared with putting everyone on Pro: put the ${creators} builder${creators === 1 ? "" : "s"} on PPU and keep ${viewers} viewer${viewers === 1 ? "" : "s"} on Pro.`;
    } else {
      verdict.innerHTML = `<strong>All Premium Per User</strong> at ${money(PRICE.ppu * total * 12)} a year.`;
    }
  }

  ["creators", "viewers"].forEach((id) => $(id)?.addEventListener("input", render));
  $("premium")?.addEventListener("change", render);
  render();
</script>

<style>
  .calc { padding: 56px 0 96px; }
  .page-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-accent); letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .calc h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 18px; max-width: 24ch; }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--c-text-muted);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent); padding-left: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 40px; max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .inputs { display: grid; gap: 22px; max-width: 560px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .field label { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .field input[type="number"] {
    width: 100%; padding: 11px 14px; font-size: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--c-bg); color: var(--c-text);
  }
  .field-check label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-weight: 600; }
  .field-check input { width: 18px; height: 18px; }
  .hint { font-size: 0.84rem; color: var(--c-text-dim); margin: 6px 0 0; }
  .results {
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 44px;
  }
  .results table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .results th {
    text-align: left; font-size: 0.8rem; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--c-text-dim); font-weight: 600;
    padding: 14px 16px; background: var(--c-bg-soft);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
  }
  .results td { padding: 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border); vertical-align: top; }
  .results tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .row-note { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--c-text-dim); }
  .empty { color: var(--c-text-dim); text-align: center; }
  .verdict {
    margin: 0; padding: 18px 16px; background: var(--c-bg-soft);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-border); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .checked { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--c-text-dim); margin: 10px 16px 14px; }
  .notes { max-width: 68ch; margin-bottom: 44px; }
  .notes h2, .faq h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .notes p { color: var(--c-text-muted); line-height: 1.72; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .faq { max-width: 68ch; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .faq h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 24px 0 8px; }
  .faq p { color: var(--c-text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
  .read-next { font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0 0 28px; color: var(--c-text-muted); }
  .source { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--c-text-dim); max-width: 68ch; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .calc h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; }
    .results table, .results thead, .results tbody, .results tr, .results td, .results th { display: block; }
    .results th { display: none; }
    .results td { padding: 10px 16px; }
    .results tr { padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border); }
  }
</style>
